+// Port: with frame_rate = 60, TMarDirector::direct still runs CUE_MOVE in
+// 1/120 s ticks but the calc-anim pass (cue & 2) comes every frame, twice as
+// often per second as at 30. moveSwing steps the submarine's swing there:
+// each water hit adds 0.0628 to the swing amplitude (one hit counted per
+// pass) and every pass takes 0.0094 off, and TKoopaJr stuns Bowser Jr. once
+// the amplitude reaches half its maximum. Stepped every frame, the swing
+// decayed twice as fast and a steady spray built it twice as fast, so the
+// stun no longer took the spraying it takes at 30. Step it once per 1/30 s:
+// on the calc pass of every other frame at 60 (the director counts one
+// unk5C per tick, two a frame).
+extern "C" int port_fps60_active;
+static inline bool KoopaJrSubmarinePortCalcStep()
+{
+	return !port_fps60_active || (gpMarDirector->unk5C & 2) != 0;
+}
+#endif
